docs\import_export_strategy.md:5:deterministic, and schema-neutral: codecs map external formats onto existing
docs\import_export_strategy.md:11:- `MarkdownCodec` supports headings, paragraphs, quotes, unordered/ordered/task
docs\import_export_strategy.md:12:  lists, fenced code, GFM pipe tables, dividers, links, inline emphasis, inline
docs\import_export_strategy.md:13:  images, standalone images, Wenz video placeholders, and readable fallbacks for
docs\import_export_strategy.md:14:  file blocks, block embeds, and custom inline embeds.
docs\import_export_strategy.md:15:- `HtmlCodec` supports headings, paragraphs, quotes, lists/tasks, code blocks,
docs\import_export_strategy.md:17:  block images, inline images, video blocks, Wenz file blocks, block embeds,
docs\import_export_strategy.md:19:- Both codecs are lenient on import: malformed or unknown content falls back to
docs\import_export_strategy.md:24:- HTML inline image embeds now round-trip `assetId`, `altText`, optional
docs\import_export_strategy.md:25:  `caption`, and optional `width`/`height` through `<img>` attributes.
docs\import_export_strategy.md:26:- Caption is exported on inline `<img>` as both `title` and `data-caption`; import
docs\import_export_strategy.md:27:  accepts `data-caption` first, then `title` as the fallback.
docs\import_export_strategy.md:28:- Block-level `<img>` import also accepts `data-caption`/`title` when no
docs\import_export_strategy.md:29:  surrounding `<figure><figcaption>` is present.
docs\import_export_strategy.md:30:- Wenz HTML file blocks now import from `<a data-wenz-block="file">`, preserving
docs\import_export_strategy.md:31:  `assetId`, display name, size, MIME type, local file, download URL, upload
docs\import_export_strategy.md:34:  Wenz `data-asset-id`/`data-file` attributes preserving round-trip metadata.
docs\import_export_strategy.md:41:  import back to `VideoBlockNode`; file blocks export as ordinary links and
docs\import_export_strategy.md:43:  an attachment.
